[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:By Heart]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.51]Lesson 22 | 第22课
[00:02.55]By heart | 熟记台词
[00:09.44]Which actor read the letter in the end, the aristocrat or the gaoler? | 最后读信的是哪位演员——贵族还是狱卒？
[00:17.32]Some plays are so successful that they run for years on end. | 有些剧目十分成功，连续上演几年都是座无虚席。
[00:22.41]In many ways, this is unfortunate for the poor actors who are required to go on repeating the same lines night after night. | 在许多方面，这可使可怜的演员们倒霉，他们得夜复一夜地重复同样的台词。
[00:32.97]One would expect them to know their parts by heart and never have cause to falter. | 人们以为演员们一定会把台词背得烂熟，绝不会临场结巴。
[00:39.12]Yet this is not always the case. | 但情况并非总是如此。
[00:42.81]A famous actor in a highly successful play was once cast in the role of an aristocrat who had been imprisoned in the Bastille for twenty years. | 有一位名演员曾在一出极为成功的剧目中扮演一个贵族，该贵族被关在巴士底狱长达20年。
[00:54.25]In the last act, a gaoler would always come on to the stage with a letter which he would hand to the prisoner. | 在最后一幕中，狱卒手持一封信上场，然后将信交给狱中的贵族。
[01:03.38]Even though the noble was expected to read the letter at each performance, he always insisted that it should be written out in full. | 尽管那个贵族每场戏都得念那封信，但他始终坚持要求将信全文写出。
[01:12.81]One night, the gaoler decided to play a joke on his colleague to find out if, | 一天晚上，狱卒决定跟他的同事开个玩笑，看看在演了这么多次之后，
[01:18.41]after so many performances, he had managed to learn the contents of the letter by heart. | 他是否已经把信的内容记熟了。
[01:25.45]The curtain went up on the final act of the play and revealed the aristocrat sitting alone behind bars in his dark cell. | 最后一幕戏开演，幕布拉开，贵族独自坐在铁栏后黑暗的牢房里。
[01:35.16]Just then, the gaoler appeared with the precious letter in his hands. | 这时狱卒上场，手里拿着那封珍贵的信。
[01:40.55]He entered the cell and presented the letter to the aristocrat. | 狱卒走进牢房，将信交给贵族。
[01:45.36]But the copy he gave him had not been written out in full as usual. | 但这一次他交给贵族的信并未像往常那样全文写出。
[01:50.50]It was simply a blank sheet of paper. | 那只是一张白纸。
[01:54.14]The gaoler looked on eagerly, anxious to see if his fellow actor had at last learnt his lines. | 狱卒热切地观察着，急于想知道他的同事是否终于记熟了台词。
[02:02.23]The noble stared at the blank sheet of paper for a few seconds. | 贵族盯着那张白纸看了几秒钟。
[02:07.45]Then, squinting his eyes, he said: 'The light is dim. Read the letter to me.' | 然后，他眯起眼睛说道：“光线太暗，请给我读一下这封信。”
[02:16.04]And he promptly handed the sheet of paper to the gaoler. | 说完，他一下子把纸递给了狱卒。
[02:20.49]Finding that he could not remember a word of the letter either, | 狱卒发现自己连信上的一个字也想不起来，
[02:24.83]the gaoler replied: 'The light is indeed dim, sire.  I must get my glasses.  ' | 便回答说：“光线确实太暗了，老爷，我得去把眼镜取来。”
[02:32.56]With this, he hurried off the stage. | 说完，他匆匆下台。
[02:36.38]Much to the aristocrat's amusement, | 令贵族感到非常好笑的是，
[02:38.83]the gaoler returned a few moments later with a pair of glasses and the usual copy of the letter which he proceeded to read to the prisoner. | 一会儿工夫狱卒便取回眼镜，还带来了往常那封写有全文的信，念给囚犯听。
